adow-main-columns\">\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-left\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-10400-ingredients\" class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-10400-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"10400\" data-servings=\"4\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">lbs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Chicken pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Your choice of wings or thighs</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Buttermilk</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For soaking the chicken</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">large</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Eggs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Beaten</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Flour</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For coating</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To taste</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For seasoning</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Paprika</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To add flavor and color</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Garlic powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For extra zest</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Hot sauce</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Adjust for your spice preference</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Honey</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To sweeten the heat</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Vegetable oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For frying, enough for about 2 inches in the pan</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-10400-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10400\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Deep Skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For frying the chicken</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Mixing bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For marinating the chicken</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Small saucepan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For making the honey hot sauce</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-10400-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-10400-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10400\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">In a bowl, whisk together buttermilk, eggs, hot sauce, salt, pepper, paprika, and garlic powder until well combined.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Add the chicken pieces to the marinade, cover the bowl, and let it marinate in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">In another bowl, pour in the flour. This will be your crispy coating!</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Heat vegetable oil in a deep skillet to 350°F (175°C).</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Take each marinated chicken piece and dredge it in the flour, shaking off any excess.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Fry the chicken in batches until golden brown and cooked through, about 8–10 minutes per side.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">In a small saucepan, warm honey and additional hot sauce over low heat, stirring until well combined.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Toss the fried chicken in the honey-hot sauce mixture until each piece is evenly coated.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10400-step-0-8\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Serve the honey hot chicken immediately. Enjoy the crispy, spicy, and sweet flavors!</div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      \n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these delightful ingredients to create your mouthwatering <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Honey\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">honey hot</a> chicken!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Honey-Hot-Chicken.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for honey hot chicken displayed on a kitchen table, including chicken, buttermilk, eggs, flour, and spices.\" class=\"wp-image-10398\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Honey-Hot-Chicken.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Honey-Hot-Chicken-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Chicken pieces</strong> – 2 lbs, your choice of wings or thighs</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Buttermilk</strong> – 1 cup, for soaking the chicken</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Eggs</strong> – 2 large, beaten</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Flour</strong> – 1 cup, for coating</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt</strong> – 1 tsp, to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Pepper</strong> – 1 tsp, for seasoning</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Paprika</strong> – 1 tsp, to add flavor and color</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Garlic powder</strong> – 1 tsp, for extra zest</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Hot sauce</strong> – 2 tbsp, adjust for your spice preference</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Honey</strong> – 1/4 cup, to sweeten the heat</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Vegetable oil</strong> – for frying, enough for about 2 inches in the pan</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-honey-hot-chicken\"><strong>How to Make Honey Hot Chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to dive into a delicious adventure! This honey hot chicken recipe takes about 1 hour for marinating, 20 minutes for cooking, and a little extra time for the flavors to meld. Let’s get cooking!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Honey-Hot-Chicken-Preparation-Steps.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making honey hot chicken, including marinade, marinating chicken, preparing flour, and frying chicken.\" class=\"wp-image-10399\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Honey-Hot-Chicken-Preparation-Steps.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Honey-Hot-Chicken-Preparation-Steps-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Whisk the Marinade</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, whisk together buttermilk, eggs, hot sauce, salt, pepper, paprika, and garlic powder until well combined.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Marinate the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the chicken pieces to the marinade, cover the bowl, and let it marinate in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour. This step is crucial for flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Prepare the Flour</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In another bowl, pour in the flour. This will be your crispy coating!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Heat the Oil</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat vegetable oil in a deep skillet to 350°F (175°C). You want it hot and ready for frying!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Dredge the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Take each marinated chicken piece and dredge it in the flour, shaking off any excess. Get that coating nice and even!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Fry the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fry the chicken in batches until golden brown and cooked through, about 8–10 minutes per side. Keep an eye on that timer!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Make the Honey Hot Sauce</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a small saucepan, warm honey and additional hot sauce over low heat, stirring until well combined. This is where the magic happens!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Toss the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Toss the fried chicken in the honey-hot sauce mixture until each piece is evenly coated. Get ready for that sweet and spicy goodness!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 9: Serve and Enjoy!</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve the honey hot chicken immediately. Enjoy the crispy, spicy, and sweet flavors!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>60 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>80 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Not specified</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Immediately after frying</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-honey-hot-chicken\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Honey Hot Chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Marinate the chicken overnight for deeper flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adjust the heat by varying the amount of hot sauce.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use honey from local sources for a unique taste.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Fry the chicken in batches to maintain oil temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the chicken rest before serving for juiciness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-honey-hot-chicken\"><strong>How to Serve this honey hot chicken</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve on a fluffy biscuit for a Southern twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with creamy coleslaw for a crunchy contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top a fresh salad with honey hot chicken for a zesty kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with sweet potato fries for a delightful combo.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in a tortilla with avocado and lettuce for a spicy burrito.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside cornbread for a comforting meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with fresh herbs for a pop of color and flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your honey hot chicken later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow chicken to cool to room temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap chicken tightly in plastic wrap or foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw chicken in the refrigerator overnight.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in the oven at 350°F (175°C) for 15-20 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For a crispy texture, use an air fryer for 5-7 minutes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1767196111646\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What exactly is hot honey chicken?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Hot honey chicken is a delicious dish that combines crispy fried chicken with a sweet and spicy glaze made from honey and hot sauce. The contrast of flavors creates a mouthwatering experience that is both savory and sweet, making it a favorite among many. This dish is perfect for those who enjoy a little kick in their meals!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-1767196125034\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What is honey, hot sauce made of?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Honey hot sauce is typically made from a blend of honey, your choice of hot sauce, and sometimes additional ingredients like vinegar, garlic, or spices to enhance the flavor. The combination of sweet honey and spicy hot sauce creates a unique and irresistible flavor profile that pairs perfectly with chicken and other dishes!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-1767196130234\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Is honey good with hot chicken?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Honey adds a delightful sweetness that balances the heat from the hot sauce, making it a perfect complement to spicy chicken. This combination not only enhances the flavor but also adds a sticky, glaze-like texture that makes the chicken even more enjoyable. It’s a match made in culinary heaven!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-1767196143954\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How to cook chicken in hot honey?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To cook chicken in hot honey, start by marinating your chicken pieces in a mixture of hot sauce and honey for at least 30 minutes. Then, cook the chicken by frying, baking, or grilling until it’s fully cooked and crispy. Once done, drizzle more hot honey over the chicken for an extra kick of flavor. Serve it hot and enjoy the delicious blend of sweet and spicy!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to savor the delightful crunch and sweet heat of honey hot chicken! This dish is not just a meal; it’s a celebration of flavors that’s easy to whip up. So gather your loved ones, dive into this recipe, and enjoy every bite. Trust me, once you try it, you’ll be hooked!</p>\n",
